Track 3: Klokwork Kolo, Vetrina Style
- Story & Context: The annual Solstice festival in Vetrina was always a riot of color and sound, but the year Buoy & Bell debuted "Klokwork Kolo," something shifted; the entire town, from the oldest fisherfolk to the youngest children, danced in a synchronized, joyous frenzy, their steps perfectly aligned to the song's intricate, almost hypnotic rhythm. Legend says the meteorite fragments in Kosta's drum machine vibrated in harmony with the ancient clock tower, causing a brief, shimmering distortion in time, making the sunset last an extra hour. "Feel the pulse, let the sun linger," became the festival's unofficial motto, as the scent of grilling fish mixed with the metallic tang of the coastal air.
